DashFloat bundles the lksctp-tools shared library (libsctp.so.1) in the Linux
release. It is unmodified, redistributed under the GNU Lesser General Public
License, version 2.1 or later.

  Upstream:  lksctp-tools — https://github.com/sctp/lksctp-tools/
  Copyright: 2001, 2003, 2005 IBM Corp.
             2001-2003 Intel Corp.
             and other contributors, see the upstream source for the full list

The library is a separate, replaceable file on disk (lib/sctp/libsctp.so.1), so
it can be substituted with any compatible build of the same library — which is
what the LGPL's relinking requirement asks for.

The GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 is available at
https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html, and its full text ships
with any distribution that packages this library (on Debian-based systems:
/usr/share/common-licenses/LGPL-2.1).

DashFloat itself does not link against this library; the Erlang VM loads it at
startup only to probe for SCTP socket support, which DashFloat does not use.
